{"title":"2017 Indonesia MO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a line passing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is either the sum or the difference of the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Five people are gathered in a meeting. Some pairs of people shakes hands. An ordered triple of people <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bc7a66472f14d58d96e940db6ebc9f101b08e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B,C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> is a trio if one of the following is true:\n</p>\n<ul><li>A shakes hands with B, and B shakes hands with C, or</li>\n<li>A doesn't shake hands with B, and B doesn't shake hands with C.</li></ul>\n<p>If we consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bc7a66472f14d58d96e940db6ebc9f101b08e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B,C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/2479f1194c589ffeb79e4a2f237e2184e526b51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(C,B,A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> as the same trio, find the minimum possible number of trios.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is special if every integer can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78ca670945d648f0b04f581fda4896313261adc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 - dc^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" /> for some integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Find the smallest positive integer that is not special.</li>\n<li>Prove 2017 is special.</li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine all pairs of distinct real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> such that both of the following are true:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10df4ca3b822bddba4a7b3efe1846aa39694c338.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x^{100} - y^{100} &amp;= 2^{99} (x-y) \\\\ x^{200} - y^{200} &amp;= 2^{199} (x-y) \\end{align*}\" width=\"192\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has integral coefficients, and it has at least 9 different integral roots. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be an integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a52bcc09031c72fd3b4fb20e1212bcc58a296f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|P(n)| &lt; 2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c2503b88124ad06581a453d02432e8ae2f27d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find the number of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> not greater than 2017 such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/b/e8b21f6594bd0eee4ba27237ecaae78e4d40988e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^n + 17k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a parallelogram. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff549161baf57bd220884df981b3b412cc50f848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC, CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> respectively such that the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a3f0e3dd12e6a4cc523abc05db1a2bce99298d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> have the same area. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d0422c6453cb48f24f5531f1598fa4f2e26ea30b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE, AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec00004a5113b974f70a8e26c3781261e56464e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M, N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. Prove there exists a triangle whose side lengths are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b084418263ed80ffd50e2eb738282d0af6e7a8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM, MN, ND$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A field is made of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/e/e1e254d48cb3b32d3ecfc51727496168e1e2f164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2017 \\times 2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" /> unit squares. Luffy has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> gold detectors, which he places on some of the unit squares, then he leaves the area. Sanji then chooses a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4c8188c12d3cbebe157aac6e18e0c1818f8b80f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1500 \\times 1500$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" /> area, then buries a gold coin on each unit square in this area and none other. When Luffy returns, a gold detector beeps if and only if there is a gold coin buried underneath the unit square it's on. It turns out that by an appropriate placement, Luffy will always be able to determine the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4c8188c12d3cbebe157aac6e18e0c1818f8b80f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1500 \\times 1500$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" /> area containing the gold coins by observing the detectors, no matter how Sanji places the gold coins. Determine the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in which this is possible.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO\">2017 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_Indonesia_MO&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 Indonesia MO (page does not exist)\">2016 Indonesia MO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_Indonesia_MO&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2018 Indonesia MO (page does not exist)\">2018 Indonesia MO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018061629\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 265/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 986/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 82/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7048/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.696      1 Template:Indonesia_MO_box\n100.00%    6.696      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16642:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018061629 and revision id 97207. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}